{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0207","billNumberShort":"H.B. 207","billNumberLong":"HB0207S02","fileNumber":"2026FL0926","shortTitle":"Competency Amendments","currentSubVersion":"2","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"ABBOTN","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Abbott, Nelson T.","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"WEILET","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Weiler, Todd","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill amends provisions related to competency evaluations.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>requires that when a court orders two competency evaluations, the evaluations must be ordered in the same order; <hr><ltbullet>provides that a court may order the Department of Health and Human Services to conduct additional or updated competency evaluations under certain circumstances;<hr><ltbullet>permits a defendant to be transferred to a clinical or inpatient setting for a competency evaluation;<hr><ltbullet>clarifies that certain provisions do not apply to progress toward competency evaluations;<hr><ltbullet>amends a provision related to a report of a progress toward competency evaluation; <hr><ltbullet>provides for the portability of an involuntary medication order when an individual is transferred between facilities; <hr><ltbullet>defines terms; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Amy Shewan","fiscalAnalyst":"Joseph Fitzgerald","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/17/2026","trackingID":"FXPMPHWIJP","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-09 12:30:47.737","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Cou